-description: "Torch 2.9 Inductor max-autotune Triton GEMM templates wrap the 32-bit A-load offset once rows × GEMM input width exceeds 2^31 while the size argument stays int32 (measured at widths 4096, 768 and 512 and silent in the real trunk; output-wide GEMMs stayed correct to 2^32); this caused the reference PPO-from-BC crash. At `1ddc71d` the rebuilt trunk guard was measured correct at L−1 and rejected L; the packed path now chunks instead of rejecting (CPU-tested). Task 3.1 registers the model and dispatches the guarded trunk compile (CPU-tested); production compliance is unproven."
